hadiths[49]{hadithnumber,text}:
"26955","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: And Hafsah narrated to me, and it was an hour in which no one entered upon him, that he used to pray two rakahs when dawn rose, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the caller would call the prayer. Ayyub said: I think he said: Two light ones."
"26956","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydillah, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, from Hafsah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is with people, they released ihram while you did not release from your umrah. He said: I have garlanded my sacrificial animal and matted my head, so I shall not release until I release from Hajj."
"26957","Surayj and Affan and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Ubaydillah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he saw Ibn Said in a lane of the lanes of Madinah, and Ibn Umar insulted him and attacked him, and he swelled until he blocked the road, so Ibn Umar struck him with a stick with him until he broke it on him. Hafsah said to him: What is with you and with him, why do you persist with him, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Dajjal only comes out of an anger he gets angry. Affan said: At an anger he gets angry. And Yunus said in his hadith: What is your persistence with him."
"26958","Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I met Ibn Said twice. As for once, I met him with some of his companions, and I said to some of them: I adjure you by Allah, if I ask you about something will you tell me truthfully. They said: Yes. He said: I said: Do you tell me that it is he. They said: No. I said: You lie, by Allah, one of you told me, while he was then the least of you in wealth and children, that he will not die until he is the most of you in wealth and children, and he is today so. He said: So he narrated to us, then I parted from him. Then I met him another time with his eye changed, and I said: When did your eye do what I see. He said: I do not know. I said: You do not know though it is in your head. He said: What do you want from me, O Ibn Umar, if Allah Almighty wills to create him from this stick of yours, He creates him. And he snorted like the hardest snort of a donkey I ever heard. Some of my companions claimed that I struck him with a stick with me until it broke, but as for me, by Allah, I did not feel it. So he entered upon his sister Hafsah and informed her, and she said: What do you want from him, do you not know that he said, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): His first emergence upon people is from an anger he gets angry. Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I met Ibn Said twice, and he mentioned the hadith, except he said: So I entered upon Hafsah, Mother of the Believers, and informed her. She said: What did you want with him, do you not know that he said: His first emergence upon people is an anger he gets angry."
"26959","Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I met Ibn Said twice. As for once, I met him with his companions, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: And he snorted like the hardest snort of a donkey I heard. He said: My companions claimed that I struck him with a stick with me until it broke, but as for me, I did not feel that. So I entered upon my sister Hafsah, Mother of the Believers, and informed her of that, and she said: And what did you want with him, do you not know that he said: His first emergence upon people is for an anger he gets angry."
"26960","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me another time, Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I met Ibn Said twice. As for once, I met him with his companions, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: And he snorted like the hardest snort of a donkey I heard. He said: Some of my companions claimed that I struck him with a stick with me until it broke, but as for me, I did not feel that. So I entered upon my sister Hafsah, Mother of the Believers, and informed her of that, and she said: And what did you want with him. Do you not know that he said: His first emergence upon people is an anger he gets angry."
"26961","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Nafi, from Abdillah ibn Umar, that Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the muadhdhin fell silent from the dawn call and dawn appeared, would pray two light rakahs before the prayer was established."
"26962","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Khattabi narrated to us in the year two hundred and eight, he said: Ubaydillah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, meaning al-Jazari, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Hafsah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the muadhdhin called, would pray two rakahs and would forbid food, and he would not call until dawn rose."
"26963","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Hafsah informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two light rakahs when dawn appeared."
"26964","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Hafsah, that she said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Why have you not released from your umrah. He said: I have matted my head and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I shall not release until I sacrifice."
"26965","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Muhammad, he said: I heard Nafia narrate from Ibn Umar, from Hafsah, that she said: When dawn rose, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray only two light rakahs."
"26966","Hisham ibn Said, meaning al-Talaqani, narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, Nafi narrated to us that Ibn Umar informed him that Hafsah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two light rakahs between the call and the iqamah of the dawn prayer."
"26967","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Jafar, meaning Ibn Burqan, narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that Hafsah informed him. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to release ihram in his Hajj which he performed. And Kathir ibn Murrah said that Ibn Umar informed him."
"26968","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb, meaning Ibn Abi Hamzah, narrated to us, he said: Nafi said: Abdillah ibn Umar used to say: Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his wives to release ihram in the year of the Farewell Hajj, and so-and-so said to him: What prevents you from releasing. He said: I have matted my head and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I shall not release until I sacrifice my sacrificial animal."
"26969","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Umar, from Hafsah daughter of Umar, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded his women to release with an umrah, they said: What prevents you, O Messenger of Allah, from releasing with us. He said: I have brought a sacrificial animal and matted, so I shall not release until I sacrifice my sacrificial animal. And Yaqub said in the book of Hajj: I sacrifice my offering."
"26970","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: He narrated to me about the two rakahs after dawn before dawn prayer: Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Hafsah daughter of Umar, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the two rakahs of dawn before dawn prayer in my house, lightening them greatly. Nafi said: And Abdullah used to lighten them likewise."
"26971","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Zayd, meaning Ibn Jubayr, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, and a man asked him what a muhrim kills of beasts. He said: One of the women narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He kills the kite and the crow and the vicious dog and the mouse and the scorpion."
"26972","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from Umm Mubashshir, from Hafsah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope that none who witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyah will enter the Fire, if Allah wills. She said: I said: Does not Allah Almighty say: There is none of you but will come to it. He said: So I heard him say: Then We shall save those who feared and leave the wrongdoers in it kneeling."
"26973","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah, from Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray his supererogatory prayer sitting at all until a year or two before his death, then he would pray his supererogatory prayer sitting and recite the surah and chant it until it is longer than longer than it."
"26974","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, and Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah, from Hafsah, she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray his supererogatory prayer sitting at all until a year before his death, then he would pray sitting and recite the surah and chant it until it is longer than longer than it."
"26975","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab said, and Ata ibn Yazid informed me that al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah informed him that Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him. She said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray sitting until a year or two before his death."
"26976","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Umayyah ibn Safwan, meaning Ibn Abdillah ibn Safwan, from his grandfather, from Hafsah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An army will surely come to this House to raid it, until when they are at al-Bayda their middle will be swallowed, and their first will call their last, and none will escape except the lone one who informs of them. A man said: Thus, by Allah, I did not lie about Hafsah, nor did Hafsah lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"26977","Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu al-Duha, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Hafsah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take from the face of some of his wives while fasting."
"26978","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Muslim, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Hafsah daughter of Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting."
"26979","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Muslim, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Hafsah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting."
"26980","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur and al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Hafsah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting."
"26981","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman, from Hafsah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while with her was a woman called Shaffa who treated ant bites with ruqyah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Teach her, O Hafsah."
"26982","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from Hafsah, that a woman of Quraysh called al-Shiffa used to treat ant bites with ruqyah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Teach her, O Hafsah."
"26983","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Umar, and he is al-Jumahi, informed us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, that one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I know her only as Hafsah, was asked about the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: You cannot bear it. She said: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful, meaning chanting."
"26984","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Nafi, that Safiyyah daughter of Abu Ubayd informed him that she heard Hafsah daughter of Umar, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day, or in Allah and His Messenger, to mourn over a dead one more than three except over a husband."
"26985","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, that Safiyyah daughter of Abu Ubayd informed him that she heard Hafsah daughter of Umar, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day, or believes in Allah and His Messenger, to mourn over a dead one more than three except over a husband, for she mourns over him four months and ten."
"26986","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Nafi, from Safiyyah daughter of Abu Ubayd, from Aishah or Hafsah, Mother of the Believers, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead one more than three except over a husband."
"26987","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Nafi, that Safiyyah daughter of Abu Ubayd narrated to him, from Hafsah or Aishah, or from both of them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day, or believes in Allah and His Messenger, to mourn over a dead one more than three days except over her husband."
"26988","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Nafi, that Safiyyah daughter of Abu Ubayd narrated to him, from Hafsah or Aishah, or from both of them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn more than three except over her husband."
"26989","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Hafsah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever does not resolve fasting with dawn, there is no fast for him."
"26990","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi, and he is the son-in-law of Salamah al-Abrash, narrated to us, he said: Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Musa, from Abdillah ibn Safwan, from Hafsah daughter of Umar, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An army will come from the east intending a man of the people of Makkah, until when they are at al-Bayda they will be swallowed, and whoever was ahead of them will return to look what the people did, and the like of what befell them will befall him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then what of one of them who was coerced. He said: All of them will be struck that, then Allah will raise every person on his intention."
"26991","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Ashjai al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai narrated to us, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Hunaydah ibn Khalid al-Khuzai, from Hafsah, she said: Four the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left: fasting Ashura, and the ten, and three days of every month, and the two rakahs before dawn."
"26992","Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Sawa al-Khuzai, from Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days of every month: Monday, and Thursday, and Monday of the other week."
"26993","Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Asim, from al-Musayyab, from Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his bed, he placed his right hand under his right cheek, and his right was for his food and purification and prayer and clothes, and his left was for other than that, and he used to fast Monday and Thursday."
"26994","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Sawa al-Khuzai, from Hafsah daughter of Umar, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed, he placed his right hand under his cheek and said: My Lord, shield me from Your punishment on the day You raise Your servants, three times."
"26995","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Sawa al-Khuzai, from Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days of every month: Monday, and Thursday, and Monday of the other week."
"26996","Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, from Sawa al-Khuzai, from Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed, he lay on his right hand, then said: My Lord, shield me from Your punishment on the day You raise Your servants, three times, and he would make his right for his eating and drinking and ablution and clothes and taking and giving, and make his left for other than that, and he used to fast three days of every month: Monday, and Thursday, and Monday of the other week."
"26997","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Aban, meaning Ibn Yazid al-Attar, narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Sawa al-Khuzai, from Hafsah daughter of Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to sleep, placed his right hand under his right cheek, then said: O Allah, shield me from Your punishment on the day You raise Your servants, three times."
"26998","And his right hand was for his food and drink, and his left hand was for the rest of his need."
"26999","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid informed me, from Abdillah ibn Abi Said al-Muzani, he said: Hafsah daughter of Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to me, she said: One day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had placed his garment between his thighs, then Abu Bakr came and asked permission, and he permitted him while on his state, then Umar likewise, then Ali, then people of his companions, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on his state, then Uthman came and asked permission, and he permitted him, then he took his garment and wrapped himself. They talked then went out. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr and Umar and Ali and the rest of your companions came while you were on your state, and when Uthman came you wrapped yourself with your garment. He said: Shall I not be shy of one whom the angels are shy of."
"27000","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Abu al-Yafur, from Abdillah ibn Abi Said al-Muzani, from Hafsah daughter of Umar, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me one day and placed his garment between his thighs, then Abu Bakr came asking permission, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him on his state, then Umar came asking permission and he permitted him while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on his state, and people of his companions came and he permitted them, and Ali came asking permission and he permitted him while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on his state, then Uthman came and asked permission, so he wrapped his garment then permitted him. They talked a while then went out. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr and Umar and Ali and people of your companions came in to you while you were on your state and you did not move, and when Uthman entered you wrapped your garment. He said: Shall I not be shy of one whom the angels are shy of."
"27001","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Al-Hurr ibn As-Sayyah narrated to us, from Hunaydah ibn Khalid, from his wife, from one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast the nine of Dhul-Hijjah and the day of Ashura and three days of every month, the first Monday of the month and two Thursdays."
"27002","Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Kamil and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Affan said in his hadith: Anas ibn Sirin informed us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Hafsah, that Utarid ibn Hajib came with a garment of dibaj which Kisra had given him as a gift, so Umar said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), if only you bought it, so he said: Only one who has no share wears it."
"27003","Waki narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Umar, and Abu Amir, Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Amir said, Nafi said: I think it is Hafsah, that she was asked about the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: You cannot manage it, he said: It was said to her: Inform us of it, he said: So she recited a recitation in which she spoke slowly, Abu Amir said, Nafi said: So Ibn Abi Mulaykah demonstrated to us: Alhamdu lillahi Rabbil-alamin, then he paused, Ar-Rahmanir-Rahim, then he paused, Maliki yawmid-din."
